#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""#4540 — the store writes the land needs, DRY RUN ONLY (Silas, for Kade).
# @domain: pipelines

Reads the live rows through the door, compares them with what #4540 needs
(the chorus-make fixtures in platform/services/chorus-make/tests/fixtures),
and prints each write as ADD / CHANGE / SAME. It writes nothing: every
store write at the land is a prod write and waits for Jeff's yes. Exit 0 =
plan printed; 2 = the door could not be read (no plan is guessed).

Every row goes through the door (Kade 07:00): the card changes only the
TBox (pipelines-4040.ttl, werk-domains.ttl, already in MODEL_SET), and no
instance file. The rows below are the ones the files would hold, embedded as
text, diffed against origin/main so only this card's subjects are written.
Order at the land: the athena run (TBox) first, so the door serves the new
fields and /testtypes; then Skills, Pipelines, PipelineSteps, TestTypes,
StepSkills, with the cicd-test-1 CHANGE last, so cicd never calls a child
that is not there yet. Applying is a separate, Jeff-approved step.
"""
